{"availability":"available","full":"ncg777/gaterunner","name":"gaterunner","description":"An experimental sequencer webapp based on the binary representation of sequences of integers with a synth, a drum machine and effects. It can export to MIDI and WAV and output real time midi.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2025-01-05T23:02:44Z","updated":"2026-10-07T20:59:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ncg777.github.io/gaterunner/","topics":["algorithmic-music","github-pages","pwa","sequencer","webaudio","webmidi"],"demo":"https://ncg777.github.io/gaterunner/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:26:14.356Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:26:14.356Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:26:14.356Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:26:14.356Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["GateRunner turns short sequences of integers into playable, evolving harmony. Each integer is a bitmask over a Forte-number pitch-class set, so one compact value can describe a note or an entire chord. Build multitrack patterns in the browser, shape them with the built-in tonewheel synth and effects, then export the result as MIDI, WAV, a reusable preset, or a shareable URL.","Algorithmic composition often means choosing between writing custom music code and manually programming a DAW. GateRunner provides a smaller feedback loop: type a numeric pattern, immediately hear how it maps onto a pitch-class set, change its rhythm or sound, and export the useful result."],"features":["Sketching chord progressions and arpeggios from compact numeric sequences.","Exploring Forte pitch-class sets without calculating every voicing by hand.","Building polymetric melodic and rhythmic loops with independent track timing.","Creating deterministic MIDI or WAV fixtures from the command line.","Designing animated tonewheel and spectral sounds directly in the browser."],"sour